a config file with a typo in it must not be a config that grants MORE.

-- an unknown policy name is ignored, leaving the default
  read: auto
  local: confirm
  external: confirm

-- a non-record scope is no scope at all
  read: auto
  local: confirm
  external: confirm

-- an unknown TIER key is ignored rather than invented
  read: auto
  local: confirm
  external: confirm

-- and an unreadable policy ranks as the strictest thing there is
  stored as: sideways
  decide -> denied (the local tier is denied by policy)
  deny (a tier that does not exist)
